# Unified Service Scheduler -- end-to-end booking flow.
#
# For the VS Code REST Client extension. Run the requests top to bottom; each
# captures the ids the next one needs, so no manual copying is required.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   cd apps/api && pnpm prisma migrate deploy && pnpm db:seed && pnpm start:dev

@host = http://localhost:3000
@contentType = application/json

### Health -- is the service up?
GET {{host}}/health

### Readiness -- is the database reachable?
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### 1. List dealerships. Northgate Auto is the interesting one: only a single
###    bay in its estate can take a transmission job, so it is where contention
###    is demonstrable.
# @name dealerships
GET {{host}}/dealerships

@dealershipId = {{dealerships.response.body.data.1.id}}

### 2. List service types. Transmission Repair runs 240 minutes, long enough
###    that one booking removes most of the day.
# @name serviceTypes
GET {{host}}/service-types

@serviceTypeId = {{serviceTypes.response.body.data.4.id}}

### 3. Pick a customer and one of their vehicles.
###    Replace the id below with one printed by `pnpm db:seed`.
@customerId = REPLACE_WITH_SEEDED_CUSTOMER_ID

# @name vehicles
GET {{host}}/customers/{{customerId}}/vehicles

@vehicleId = {{vehicles.response.body.data.0.id}}

### 4. Availability for a Monday. Advisory only -- a slot shown free here can be
###    taken a moment later. Booking re-checks atomically.
GET {{host}}/availability?dealershipId={{dealershipId}}&serviceTypeId={{serviceTypeId}}&date=2026-09-07

### 5. Hold the 07:30 local slot for two minutes while "filling in the form".
# @name hold
POST {{host}}/holds
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealershipId}}",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{vehicleId}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceTypeId}}",
  "startAt": "2026-09-07T06:30:00Z"
}

@holdId = {{hold.response.body.data.id}}

### 6. While the hold is live, a competitor is refused. Expect 409.
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealershipId}}",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{vehicleId}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceTypeId}}",
  "startAt": "2026-09-07T06:30:00Z"
}

### 7. Confirm the hold. Promotes the SAME row to CONFIRMED -- note the id is
###    unchanged, so the slot is never momentarily released.
# @name appointment
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Idempotency-Key: walkthrough-key-001

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealershipId}}",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{vehicleId}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceTypeId}}",
  "startAt": "2026-09-07T06:30:00Z",
  "holdId": "{{holdId}}"
}

@appointmentId = {{appointment.response.body.data.id}}

### 8. Replay with the same Idempotency-Key. Same appointment, replayed: true,
###    and still exactly one row in the database.
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Idempotency-Key: walkthrough-key-001

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealershipId}}",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{vehicleId}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceTypeId}}",
  "startAt": "2026-09-07T06:30:00Z",
  "holdId": "{{holdId}}"
}

### 9. The confirmation record (Requirement 3): customer, vehicle, technician,
###    and service bay, all associated.
GET {{host}}/appointments/{{appointmentId}}

### 10. Booking someone else's vehicle is refused. Expect 403.
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealershipId}}",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "vehicleId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceTypeId}}",
  "startAt": "2026-09-08T06:30:00Z"
}

### 11. Outside opening hours. Expect 422.
POST {{host}}/appointments
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealershipId}}",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{vehicleId}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceTypeId}}",
  "startAt": "2026-09-08T03:00:00Z"
}

### 12. All appointments for the customer.
GET {{host}}/appointments?customerId={{customerId}}

### 13. Cancel. The record is retained for audit and the slot becomes bookable.
DELETE {{host}}/appointments/{{appointmentId}}

### 14. Confirm the slot came back.
GET {{host}}/availability?dealershipId={{dealershipId}}&serviceTypeId={{serviceTypeId}}&date=2026-09-07

### Domain metrics: conflicts, retry exhaustion, attempts per booking.
GET {{host}}/metrics
